# Spicy Salmon Roll Bowls

Based on [https://healthyishfoods.com/spicy-salmon-roll-bowl/…](https://healthyishfoods.com/spicy-salmon-roll-bowls) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250802235318/https://healthyishfoods.com/spicy-salmon-roll-bowls/))

{ rating="5" image="spicy_salmon_roll_bowls.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Salmon and Blackening Spice

- [ ] 12-16 oz [salmon]{ ing="salmon" }, cubed and seasoned
- [ ] 1 tsp [oregano]{ ing="oregano" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [onion powder]{ ing="onion-powder" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [paprika]{ ing="paprika" }

### Spicy Sauce

- [ ] 1/4 cup [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [sriracha]{ ing="sriracha" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }, low sodium
- [ ] 1 tsp [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }

_Alternative sauce options:_ Yum Yum sauce (mayo + ketchup + paprika + garlic powder), store-bought spicy mayo, or eel sauce mixed with sriracha

### Salmon Bowls

- [ ] 2 cups [short-grain white]{ ing="short-grain-white" } or brown rice, uncooked
- [ ] 2 [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, thin-sliced
- [ ] [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, thin-sliced
- [ ] 1/2 [avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, sliced
- [ ] 1/4 cup [peanuts or edamame]{ ing="peanuts-or-edamame" } (shelled)
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [jalapeno]{ ing="jalapeno" }, thin-sliced
- [ ] [and/or green onions]{ ing="and-or-green-onions" }, snap peas, seaweed salad, etc.

### Serving

- [ ] 2 Tbsp [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped
- [ ] 1 large [lime]{ ing="lime" }, quartered
- [ ] [toasted sesame seeds]{ ing="toasted-sesame-seeds" } or 2 tsp furikake, split between the bowls

## Recipe

1. Cook the rice
1. In small prep bowls:

   1. Combine the blackening spice
   1. Combine the [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }, [sriracha]{ ing="sriracha" }, [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }, and [sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }. Whisk until well combined
1. Chop and prep the rest of the vegetables

   1. Saute until softened
1. Remove [salmon]{ ing="salmon" } skin, then cube into bite-sized pieces

   1. Toss with the blackening spice
   1. In a skillet, pan fry the [salmon]{ ing="salmon" } for 3-4 minutes in olive oil on medium-high heat
1. Add the rice as a base, then top with the sliced [avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, chopped [green onion]{ ing="and-or-green-onions" }, sliced [jalapeno]{ ing="jalapeno" }, sliced [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, and seared [salmon]{ ing="salmon" } cubes

   1. Finish with [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, fresh squeezed [lime]{ ing="lime" }, [sesame seeds]{ ing="toasted-sesame-seeds" }/furikake, and spicy [sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }

## Notes

- **Rice options:** Traditional sushi rice (short-grain white rice) has the best sticky texture for this bowl. Brown short-grain rice can be used for higher fiber and lower glycemic impact
- **Flavor/texture tradeoff with brown rice:** Brown rice is chewier and less sticky than white sushi rice, and has a nuttier flavor. To improve stickiness when using brown rice, rinse it well and add rice vinegar after cooking (2 Tbsp rice vinegar + 1 Tbsp sugar per 2 cups uncooked rice). The vinegar helps the rice clump slightly and adds traditional sushi rice flavor
- **Protein boost:** Add shelled edamame for extra protein and fiber (5-6g protein per 1/2 cup)
- **Additional toppings:** Seaweed salad, pickled ginger, or shredded nori add authentic sushi flavors
- **Meal prep:** Cook rice and prep vegetables ahead. Sear salmon fresh for best texture, though it can be gently reheated
